.Dt QUERY-PROCESSING 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm query-processing
.Nd cara database eksekusi query, dari parsing sampai pipelining
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Ini catatan Chapter 12 dari buku Database System Concepts. Isinya:
langkah-langkah query processing, ukuran cost, algoritma selection,
sorting, join, operasi lain, dan evaluasi ekspresi.
.Pp
Bahasa santai. Tiap algoritma dijelasin kenapa dia ada dan kapan
dipakai. Karena query yang sama bisa dieksekusi dengan banyak
cara, dan bedanya bisa dari detik ke hari.
.Ss Bagian 1: Tiga Langkah Query Processing
Setiap query yang kamu kirim ke database, lewat 3 langkah:
.Bl -tag -width "Evaluation" -offset indent
.It Sy 1. Parsing dan Translation
Query diterjemahin jadi bentuk internal. Parser cek syntax,
verify relation yang disebut ada.
.It Sy 2. Optimization
Query optimizer pilih evaluation plan yang paling murah. Dari
semua cara yang equivalent, pilih yang cost-nya paling rendah.
.It Sy 3. Evaluation
Query-execution engine ambil plan, eksekusi, return hasil.
.El
.Ss Bagian 1.1: Alur Visual
.Bd -literal -offset indent
query
  |
  v
[parser and translator] --> relational-algebra expression
                                  |
                                  v
                              [optimizer] <-- statistics
                                  |
                                  v
                            execution plan
                                  |
                                  v
                        [evaluation engine] --> query output
                                  |
                                  v
                                 data
.Ed
.Sy Kenapa perlu optimizer?
Karena satu ekspresi relational algebra bisa punya banyak
bentuk equivalent. Contoh:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sigma_{salary < 75000}(pi_{salary}(instructor))
=
pi_{salary}(sigma_{salary < 75000}(instructor))
.Ed
Dua-duanya hasilnya sama, tapi cost-nya beda. Optimizer pilih
yang lebih murah.
.Ss Bagian 2: Ukuran Cost Query
.Sy Cost
= total elapsed time buat jawab query.
.Pp
.Sy Faktor yang contribute:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Disk access (paling dominant).
.It
CPU.
.It
Network communication.
.El
.Sy Kenapa disk access yang dihitung?
Karena disk access paling mahal (5-10 ms) dibanding CPU (ns)
dan paling gampang diestimasi.
.Ss Bagian 2.1: Komponen Cost
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Cost = (number of seeks) * (average seek cost)
     + (number of blocks read) * (average block read cost)
     + (number of blocks written) * (average block write cost)
.Ed
.Sy Write lebih mahal dari read.
Karena setelah write, data dibaca balik buat verifikasi bahwa
write sukses.
.Ss Bagian 2.2: Notasi
.Bl -tag -width "t_S" -offset indent
.It Sy t T
Time to transfer one block.
.It Sy t S
Time for one seek.
.It Sy b T
Total block transfer.
.It Sy S
Total seek.
.El
.Sy Cost formula:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
b * tT + S * tS
.Ed
.Sy Kita ignore CPU cost buat simplifikasi.
Real system tetap hitung, tapi disk access yang dominant.
.Pp
.Sy Buffer:
Kita pakai worst-case estimate. Asumsi cuma minimum memory
yang available. Data yang udah di buffer nggak dihitung
disk I/O-nya, tapi hard to estimate.
.Ss Bagian 3: Selection Operation
.Sy Selection
= filter baris berdasarkan kondisi. Notasi
.Sy sigma Ns _theta Ns ( Ns Ar r Ns ) .
.Ss Bagian 3.1: A1 \(em Linear Search
.Sy Algoritma:
Scan tiap block file, test semua record.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Cost = b_r block transfers + 1 seek
.Ed
.Sy Kalau selection on key attribute:
Bisa stop pas ketemu record. Cost =
.Sy b_r / 2
block transfers + 1 seek.
.Pp
.Sy Kapan dipakai:
Bisa dipakai regardless of selection condition, ordering,
atau index availability.
.Sy Binary search umumnya nggak masuk akal
karena data nggak disimpen consecutively (kecuali ada index).
.Ss Bagian 3.2: A2 \(em Primary Index, Equality on Key
.Sy Cara:
Retrieve single record yang satisfy equality.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Cost = (h_i + 1) * (tT + tS)
.Ed
.Sy h_i
= height of index.
.Ss Bagian 3.3: A3 \(em Primary Index, Equality on Non-Key
.Sy Cara:
Retrieve multiple records yang mungkin di consecutive block.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Cost = h_i * (tT + tS) + tS + tT * b
.Ed
.Sy b
= number of blocks containing matching records.
.Ss Bagian 3.4: A4 \(em Secondary Index, Equality
.Bl -tag -width "Non-key" -offset indent
.It Sy Candidate key
Retrieve single record.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Cost = (h_i + 1) * (tT + tS)
.Ed
.It Sy Non-candidate key
Setiap record bisa di block berbeda. Bisa mahal.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Cost = (h_i + n) * (tT + tS)
.Ed
.Sy n
= number of matching records.
.El
.Ss Bagian 3.5: A5 \(em Primary Index, Comparison
.Sy Sigma A >= v:
Pakai index buat temuin tuple pertama >= v, scan relation
sequentially dari situ.
.Sy Sigma A <= v:
Scan relation sequentially sampai tuple pertama > v. Jangan
pakai index.
.Ss Bagian 3.6: A6 \(em Secondary Index, Comparison
.Sy Sigma A >= v:
Pakai index buat temuin index entry pertama >= v, scan index
sequentially dari situ, temuin pointer ke records.
.Sy Sigma A <= v:
Scan leaf pages of index, temuin pointer ke records, sampai
entry pertama > v.
.Pp
.Sy Fetch records
butuh I/O per record. Linear file scan mungkin lebih murah.
.Ss Bagian 3.7: Complex Selection \(em Conjunction
.Sy AND ( \(ua ):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sigma_{theta1 and theta2 and ... and thetan}(r)
.Ed
.Sy A7 \(em Conjunctive Selection Using One Index:
Pilih kombinasi
.Sy theta i
dan algoritma A1-A7 yang paling murah. Test kondisi lain
setelah fetch ke memory buffer.
.Sy A8 \(em Composite Index:
Pakai composite (multiple-key) index kalau ada.
.Sy A9 \(em Intersection of Identifiers:
Pakai index buat tiap condition, intersect semua set of
record pointer. Fetch records dari file.
.Ss Bagian 3.8: Complex Selection \(em Disjunction
.Sy OR ( \(vu ):
.Sy A10 \(em Union of Identifiers:
Applicable kalau semua condition punya index. Pakai index
buat tiap condition, union semua set of record pointer.
Fetch records dari file. Kalau nggak ada index, pakai linear
scan.
.Ss Bagian 3.9: Complex Selection \(em Negation
.Sy NOT ( \(no ):
Pakai linear scan on file. Kalau very few records satisfy
.Sy not theta
dan index applicable buat
.Sy theta ,
temuin satisfying records pakai index, fetch dari file.
.Ss Bagian 4: Sorting
.Sy Kenapa sorting penting?
Banyak operasi database butuh sorted input:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Merge join.
.It
Duplicate elimination.
.It
Group by.
.It
Order by.
.El
.Sy Kalau relation fit di memory:
Quicksort atau teknik in-memory lain.
.Sy Kalau nggak fit:
External sort-merge.
.Ss Bagian 4.1: External Sort-Merge
.Sy Fase 1 \(em Create Sorted Runs:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
i := 0
while belum end of relation:
    read M blocks ke memory
    sort in-memory blocks
    write sorted data ke run R_i
    i := i + 1
N := nilai akhir i
.Ed
.Sy Fase 2 \(em Merge Runs (N-way merge):
Asumsi
.Sy N < M .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Gunakan N block memory buat buffer input runs
Gunakan 1 block buat buffer output
Read first block tiap run ke buffer page

repeat:
    pilih first record (in sort order) dari semua buffer
    write ke output buffer
    kalau output buffer full, write ke disk
    delete record dari input buffer
    kalau buffer page empty, read next block
until semua input buffer empty
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 4.2: Kalau N >= M
Beberapa merge pass diperlukan.
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Tiap pass, contiguous group of M-1 runs di-merge.
.It
Pass reduces number of runs by factor M-1.
.It
Contoh: M=11, 90 runs \(-> 1 pass jadi 9 runs, tiap run 10x
lebih besar.
.El
.Ss Bagian 4.3: Cost of External Sorting
.Sy Block transfers:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
b_r * (2 * ceil(log_{M/bb - 1}(b_r / M)) + 1)
.Ed
.Sy bb
= buffer blocks per run.
.Sy Seeks:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
2 * ceil(b_r / M)
+ ceil(b_r / bb) * (2 * ceil(log_{M/bb - 1}(b_r / M)) - 1)
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 5: Join Operation
.Sy Beberapa algoritma join:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Nested-loop join.
.It
Block nested-loop join.
.It
Indexed nested-loop join.
.It
Merge-join.
.It
Hash-join.
.El
.Sy Contoh data:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
student: 5,000 records, 100 blocks
takes:   10,000 records, 400 blocks
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 5.1: Nested-Loop Join
.Sy Algoritma:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
for each tuple t_r in r:
    for each tuple t_s in s:
        test pair (t_r, t_s) satisfy join condition
        kalau iya, add t_r.t_s ke result
.Ed
.Sy r
= outer relation.
.Sy s
= inner relation.
.Pp
.Sy Cost worst case:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
n_r * b_s + b_r block transfers
n_r + b_r seeks
.Ed
.Sy Kalau smaller relation fit di memory:
Pakai itu sebagai inner relation. Cost =
.Sy b_r + b_s
block transfers + 2 seeks.
.Ss Bagian 5.2: Block Nested-Loop Join
.Sy Algoritma:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
for each block B_r of r:
    for each block B_s of s:
        for each tuple t_r in B_r:
            for each tuple t_s in B_s:
                test join condition
                kalau iya, add ke result
.Ed
.Sy Cost worst case:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
b_r * b_s + b_r block transfers
2 * b_r seeks
.Ed
.Sy Best case:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
b_r + b_s block transfers + 2 seeks
.Ed
.Sy Improvement:
Pakai M-2 disk blocks as blocking unit for outer relation.
.Sy M
= memory size in blocks.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Cost = ceil(b_r / (M-2)) * b_s + b_r block transfers
     + 2 * ceil(b_r / (M-2)) seeks
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 5.3: Indexed Nested-Loop Join
.Sy Index lookups
bisa replace file scans kalau:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Join-nya equi-join atau natural join.
.It
Ada index di inner relation's join attribute.
.El
.Sy Algoritma:
Buat tiap tuple
.Sy t_r
di outer relation, pakai index buat lookup tuple
.Sy s
yang satisfy join condition.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Cost = b_r * (tT + tS) + n_r * c
.Ed
.Sy c
= cost of traversing index dan fetching matching tuple.
.Ss Bagian 5.4: Merge-Join
.Sy Langkah:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Sort kedua relation di join attribute.
.It
Merge sorted relations buat join.
.El
.Sy Main difference dari merge sort:
Handling duplicate values di join attribute. Setiap pair dengan
value sama harus di-match.
.Pp
.Sy Cost:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
b_r + b_s block transfers
+ ceil(b_r / bb) + ceil(b_s / bb) seeks
+ cost of sorting kalau unsorted
.Ed
.Sy Hybrid merge-join:
Kalau satu relation sorted, yang lain punya secondary B+ tree
index di join attribute. Merge sorted relation dengan leaf
entries of B+ tree.
.Ss Bagian 5.5: Hash-Join
.Sy Applicable buat:
Equi-join dan natural join.
.Sy Cara:
Pakai hash function
.Sy h
buat partition tuple kedua relation.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
h: JoinAttrs -> {0, 1, ..., n}

r_0, r_1, ..., r_n = partition dari r
s_0, s_1, ..., s_n = partition dari s

t_r in r_i kalau i = h(t_r[JoinAttrs])
t_s in s_i kalau i = h(t_s[JoinAttrs])
.Ed
.Sy Kenapa harus partition?
Karena r tuple di r_i cuma perlu dibandingin dengan s tuple di
s_i. Nggak perlu dibandingin dengan partition lain.
.Ss Bagian 5.6: Hash-Join Algorithm
.Bd -literal -offset indent
1. Partition relation s pakai hash function h
2. Partition relation r similarly
3. For each i:
   a. Load s_i ke memory, build in-memory hash index
      pakai join attribute
   b. Read tuple r_i dari disk satu-satu
      For each t_r, locate matching t_s di s_i
      pakai in-memory hash index
      Output concatenation
.Ed
.Sy s
= build input.
.Sy r
= probe input.
.Ss Bagian 5.7: Cost of Hash-Join
.Sy Kalau recursive partitioning nggak diperlukan:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
3 * (b_r + b_s) + 4 * n_h block transfers
2 * (ceil(b_r/bb) + ceil(b_s/bb)) seeks
.Ed
.Sy Kalau recursive partitioning diperlukan:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
2 * (b_r + b_s) * ceil(log_{M/bb - 1}(b_s / M))
+ b_r + b_s block transfers
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 5.8: Hybrid Hash-Join
.Sy Feature:
Keep first partition of build relation di memory.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Dengan memory 25 blocks:
instructor partitioned into 5 partitions, masing-masing 20 blocks
First partition occupies 20 blocks memory
1 block for input, 1 block each for buffering other 4 partitions
.Ed
.Sy Cost:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
3*(80+320) + 20 + 80 = 1300 block transfers
dibanding 1500 dengan plain hash-join
.Ed
.Sy Useful kalau M >> sqrt(b_s).
.Ss Bagian 6: Operasi Lain
.Ss Bagian 6.1: Duplicate Elimination
.Sy Via sorting:
Duplicates bakal adjacent. Semua kecuali satu bisa dihapus.
Optimization: hapus duplicates selama run generation dan
intermediate merge.
.Sy Via hashing:
Duplicates bakal masuk bucket yang sama.
.Ss Bagian 6.2: Projection
Projection on each tuple, followed by duplicate elimination.
.Ss Bagian 6.3: Aggregation
Sama seperti duplicate elimination. Sorting atau hashing
buat bawa tuple ke group yang sama.
.Sy Optimization:
Combine tuple di group yang sama during run generation dan
intermediate merges, dengan compute partial aggregate values.
.Bl -tag -width "avg" -offset indent
.It Sy count, min, max, sum
Keep aggregate value dari tuple yang udah ketemu.
.It Sy count kombinasi
Add up aggregates.
.It Sy avg
Keep sum dan count, divide at the end.
.El
.Ss Bagian 6.4: Set Operations
.Sy Union:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
1. Partition r dan s pakai same hash function
2. Process tiap partition i:
   a. Build in-memory hash index on r_i
   b. Add tuple s_i ke hash index kalau belum ada
   c. Add tuple hash index ke result
.Ed
.Sy Intersection dan Difference:
Partition dulu, build hash index on r_i. Process s_i:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
.Sy r intersect s :
Output tuple s_i kalau udah ada di hash index.
.It
.Sy r - s :
Kalau tuple s_i ada di hash index, delete dari index. Di
akhir, add remaining tuple ke result.
.El
.Ss Bagian 6.5: Outer Join
.Sy Cara 1:
Join followed by addition of null-padded non-participating
tuple.
.Sy Cara 2:
Modify join algorithms.
.Sy Merge-join modification:
During merging, buat setiap tuple
.Sy t_r
dari
.Sy r
yang nggak match, output
.Sy t_r
padded with nulls.
.Ss Bagian 7: Evaluasi Ekspresi
.Sy Dua alternatif:
.Bl -tag -width "Pipelining" -offset indent
.It Sy Materialization
Evaluate satu operasi at a time, simpen intermediate result
ke temporary relation di disk.
.It Sy Pipelining
Pass tuple ke parent operation bahkan saat operasi masih
executing.
.El
.Ss Bagian 7.1: Materialized Evaluation
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Compute dan store sigma_{building="Watson"}(department)
Compute dan store join dengan instructor
Compute projection on name
.Ed
.Sy Cost:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Sum of individual operations
+ cost of writing intermediate results to disk
.Ed
.Sy Double buffering:
Use two output buffer per operation. Ketika satu full, write
ke disk sementara yang lain filled. Overlap disk writes dengan
computation.
.Ss Bagian 7.2: Pipelining
.Sy Pipelined evaluation:
Evaluate beberapa operasi simultaneously, pass result dari
satu operasi ke next.
.Sy Contoh:
Jangan store result
.Sy sigma Ns _{building="Watson"} Ns ( Ns department Ns ) .
Pass tuple langsung ke join. Jangan store result join, pass
ke projection.
.Sy Kenapa lebih murah?
Nggak perlu store temporary relation ke disk.
.Sy Kapan nggak bisa pipelining?
Sort, hash-join \(em operasi yang butuh lihat semua input
sebelum output apapun.
.Ss Bagian 7.3: Dua Cara Pipelining
.Bl -tag -width "Producer-driven" -offset indent
.It Sy Demand-driven (lazy)
System request next tuple from top-level operation. Tiap
operasi request next tuple dari children seperlunya.
.It Sy Producer-driven (eager)
Operator produce tuple eagerly, pass ke parent. Buffer
maintained between operators.
.El
.Sy Istilah lain:
Pull model (demand-driven) dan push model (producer-driven).
.Ss Bagian 7.4: Demand-Driven Implementation
.Sy Iterator model:
Tiap operasi implement tiga operasi:
.Bl -tag -width "next()" -offset indent
.It Sy open()
Initialize. Contoh: file scan init pointer, merge join sort
relation.
.It Sy next()
Return next tuple, advance state. Contoh: file scan output
next tuple, merge join continue merge dari state sebelumnya.
.It Sy close()
Cleanup.
.El
.Ss Bagian 7.5: Pipelining di Merge/Hash Join
.Sy Masalah:
Merge join dan hash join butuh tulis intermediate result ke
disk dulu sebelum baca balik.
.Sy Solusi:
Hybrid hash join generate output tuple bahkan saat probe
relation tuple di in-memory partition (partition 0) dibaca.
.Sy Double-pipelined join:
Hybrid hash join, modified buat buffer partition 0 tuple dari
kedua relation di memory.
.Ss Ringkasan
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Konsep              Inti
Parsing             Terjemahin query ke internal form
Optimization        Pilih plan paling murah
Evaluation          Eksekusi plan
Cost                Block transfers + seeks
tT                  Time to transfer one block
tS                  Time for one seek
Selection           Filter baris
Linear search       Scan semua, A1
Index scan          Pakai index, A2-A6
Conjunction         AND, A7-A9
Disjunction         OR, A10
Negation            NOT, linear scan
External sort       Sort-merge, multi-pass
Nested-loop join    Simple, mahal
Block nested-loop   Per block, lebih murah
Indexed nested-loop Pakai index di inner
Merge-join          Sort dulu, merge
Hash-join           Partition, build, probe
Hybrid hash-join    Keep partition 0 di memory
Duplicate elim      Sorting atau hashing
Projection          Projection + dedup
Aggregation         Sort/hash, partial aggregate
Set operations      Partition + hash index
Outer join          Modify join algorithms
Materialization     Store intermediate ke disk
Pipelining          Pass tuple ke parent
Demand-driven       Pull model
Producer-driven     Push model
.Ed
Kalau kamu cuma inget satu hal dari catatan ini, inget ini:
.Sy cost query itu ditentuin sama jumlah block transfers dan
seeks. Bukan sama "rumitnya" query. Query yang keliatan simpel
bisa jadi mahal kalau algoritmanya salah. Query yang keliatan
rumit bisa jadi murah kalau pakai index dan pipelining.
.Pp
Yang belum dijawab di sini: gimana caranya optimizer milih
algoritma yang tepat? Gimana caranya estimasi cost intermediate
result? Itu topik lanjutan: query optimization (Chapter 13)
dan cost estimation. Kalau penasaran, cari sendiri.
